)PANEL KEYLIST(ISRHELP,ISR)
)ATTR DEFAULT(%+_)
/*********************************************************************/
/* PANEL    : MBKCGRH                                                */
/* TITLE    : HELP - CHARGE REFUNDS                                  */
/*-------------------------------------------------------------------*/
/* 2007-08-20 JNB  ORIGINAL                                          */
/* 2015-03-02 PDQ  FOS / HARDSHIP                                    */
/*********************************************************************/
  % TYPE(TEXT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(WHITE) SKIP(ON)
  + TYPE(TEXT) INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(GREEN) SKIP(ON)
  ] TYPE(TEXT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) SKIP(ON)
)BODY EXPAND(//) WIDTH(80)
%TUTORIAL -/-/- CHARGE REFUNDS -/-/- TUTORIAL
%Command ===>_ZCMD                                                             +
+
+A refund reverses all or part of one charge that has been applied (a row
+in MBK.CHGHIST).  Identify the charge exactly - sort code, account, period
+end, charge type and item sequence - from the Charge History enquiry.
+
]Reason codes+
+  %GDWL+goodwill            %CMPL+complaint upheld (case ref required)
+  %BERR+bank error           %FOSD+Financial Ombudsman decision (FOS... ref)
+  %HARD+financial hardship - collections referral (COL... ref)
+
]Amount+
+   Key the refund in pounds.  Zero means "whatever is left of the charge
+   after earlier refunds" - CGREF010 works it out.  Refunds can never take
+   the total refunded above the charge.
+
]Approval+
+   Requester and approver must be different users.  Over 250.00 (or a
+   zero / balance refund) the approver must be a team leader listed in
+   CGREF010 (CRTL0001 CRTL0002 CRTL0004 CRTL0007 CRMGR001 CRMGR002).
+
]Cut-off+
+   Approved refunds are released to the batch from option R, by 21:30.
+   Releasing twice in a day is safe - the second release is merged.
)PROC
  &ZUP = MBKMENUH
)END
